<!-- Taxation — the realm: tax → gold, rations → food, both → popularity → migration.

     Every realm tick a keep-holder collects tax as gold and feeds its people from
     the larder; the two settings trade against a single popularity number, and
     popularity is what draws newcomers in or drives idlers out. These tests hold
     down that the treasury fills and never goes negative, that a starving realm is
     punished however generous its ration order, that popularity moves the
     population the right way, that the SetTax/SetRations commands take, and — the
     one that matters for a match — that the whole realm is deterministic across
     two clients.

     Sim-only, like the other economy suites. Run with `dotnet run`. -->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>TaxationTests</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TaxationTests</AssemblyName>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="../../game/Sim/*.cs" LinkBase="Sim" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
